1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,710
People say saving in a dividend ETF for
years leaves more than an index ETF.

2
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:08,279
To check, we ran a
backtest with AI-written

3
00:00:08,279 --> 00:00:10,600
Python code on real past prices.

4
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:14,470
We tested SCHD, a US dividend stock ETF.

5
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:20,520
We compared it with SPY, which pays
smaller dividends but tracks the S&P 500.

6
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:24,010
From 2011, each account
got $1,000 every month.

7
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:29,240
In both accounts, every dividend had
15% tax withheld, then was reinvested.

8
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:33,270
15% is the rate withheld on US
dividends in many countries.

9
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:37,080
By 2026, each account had put in $180,000.

10
00:00:37,530 --> 00:00:43,130
The SCHD account had about $480,000;
the SPY account, about $590,000.

11
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:50,440
SCHD received 2.1 times SPY's dividends,
but SPY had 1.22 times as much money left.

12
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:53,770
More dividends, so why less money left?

13
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:59,050
Why, and whether another start month gives
the same result: see the video below.
